WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 3 Leader Video
Unit 1, Lesson 3: Truth

1
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.900
Every year, Oxford Dictionary puts out a word of the year.

2
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:23.560
The word of the year for 2016 was this.

3
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.560
Post-Truth.

4
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.560
It's an adjective.

5
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.560
It's defined as relating to or denoting circumstances

6
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:39.560
in which objective facts are less influential in shaping public opinion

7
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.560
than appeals to emotion and personal belief.

8
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.930
So in other words,

9
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:51.560
post-truth means that you don't really need to worry about objective facts

10
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.560
and it's really about how you feel about something.

11
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.560
You don't have to necessarily agree with objective truth.

12
00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.560
But your own subjective truth is much more valuable.

13
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.560
Essentially, this is the word of the year.

14
00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.560
This is exactly what we're up against or what our students are up against.

15
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.560
Every day that they walk into the classroom at school,

16
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.269
every day that they interact with their friends and they see media and movies and

17
00:01:18.269 --> 00:01:18.560
music

18
00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.560
and everything else that's on TV, this is what we're talking about.

19
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.560
It's essentially relativism, the idea that objective truth no longer matters

20
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.560
and no longer has any space in our heads to navigate our own reality.

21
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.560
In other words, if I don't like objective reality, I can just completely ignore it

22
00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.560
and not worry about it and create my own reality, my own truth.

23
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.050
You can probably already start to imagine what kind of problems this is going to

24
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.560
cause in your own mind

25
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.718
against what students,

26
00:01:52.718 --> 00:01:56.560
which is also often why we as leaders will stand in front of our students

27
00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.560
and start talking about something that we think and we know is objectively true,

28
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.560
especially what's based on Scripture.

29
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:08.560
And there's a wall between what we're saying and our students

30
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.560
because oftentimes they're looking at what we're saying and thinking,

31
00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.560
well, wait a minute, that's what you think to be true.

32
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.560
I don't accept that as true.

33
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.489
Even though we're saying that this is objectively true,

34
00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:23.560
that this is absolutely true,

35
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.560
they don't necessarily agree with it.

36
00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:32.560
See, you and I probably accepted truth for what it is, even if we didn't like it.

37
00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.560
So, okay, this is what truth is, this is the reality of the situation

38
00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.560
or the reality of our environment or the reality of our lives.

39
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.917
We may not like it,

40
00:02:39.917 --> 00:02:44.560
but we accept it and we deal with it or we change it or whatever.

41
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:50.560
Students will base their truth off of the reality that they create

42
00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.560
because they're told that's exactly what you're allowed to do.

43
00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:04.160
But it's important that you help your students see truth for what it really is.

44
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.160
This lesson is so, so important as you continue to move forward

45
00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:14.160
because you can't talk about the reality or the authority of Scripture.

46
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.160
You can't talk about the reality of the resurrection.

47
00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.160
You can't talk about the existence of God.

48
00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.160
You can't talk about the problem of evil.

49
00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:25.160
You can't talk about really anything else that you're going to dive into

50
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.160
until your students understand the nature of truth.

51
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.160
So, truth is what corresponds with reality.

52
00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.160
When you think of truth, when you help your students think of truth,

53
00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.160
sort of help them navigate away from this idea of post-truth

54
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.160
and remind them that truth is what is real, what is reality.

55
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:52.160
So, reality is really a thing that's independent of me or you or your students.

56
00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.160
So, what it is regardless of we're interacting with it or not.

57
00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:00.160
So, more than just understanding truth and reality

58
00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.160
is the understanding that genuine freedom comes by living through truth.

59
00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.160
Because remember, we're talking about what it means to have faith.

60
00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.160
We're talking about truth in that context.

61
00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.160
And our students want to be free.

62
00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.160
We want them to experience the freedom that is in Christ

63
00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.160
and that comes from understanding what truth is.

64
00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.160
And truth is what corresponds with reality.

65
00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.160
Now, it might be really attempting for them to think,

66
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.160
well, as long as it makes sense or as long as it's practical,

67
00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.160
then that's fine.

68
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.160
Then it can be true, right?

69
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.160
It can be coherent.

70
00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.160
It can be practical.

71
00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.160
It can be whatever.

72
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.160
As long as it makes sense to me, then it can be true.

73
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.160
Well, that's not necessarily the case.

74
00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.160
And if you think about it,

75
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.160
there's lots of things that are coherent.

76
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.160
Think about belief in things like Santa Claus or the Easter Bunny

77
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.160
fairy.

78
00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:53.160
When we're kids, those things make all the sense in the world.

79
00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.160
But we know that these things don't line up with reality.

80
00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:01.160
And parents may spend a lot of time making these things incredibly practical.

81
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.160
But yet they don't line up with reality.

82
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.160
And so it might make sense for some other religious beliefs

83
00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.160
or some other ideas that students may come across that sound good.

84
00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.160
Sound like they make sense.

85
00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.160
Sound very practical.

86
00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.160
That doesn't mean they line up with reality.

87
00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:24.160
You know, it might sound really nice to say all religions lead to the same place

88
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.160
or that all religions have some idea of truth to them.

89
00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.160
But then what do we do in John 14 when Jesus says,

90
00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.160
I am the way of the truth in the life.

91
00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.160
Nobody gets the Father but by me.

92
00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.160
Jesus is making an objective truth claim.

93
00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.160
So either that is true or it's not.

94
00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.160
And it doesn't matter what I think of it.

95
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.160
So either what Jesus said is true or not,

96
00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.160
whether I interact with it or not,

97
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.160
whether I believe in it or not, it's either true or it's false.

98
00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.160
That's what we call objective truth.

99
00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.160
So if what Jesus is saying is true,

100
00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:06.160
that makes every other belief that contradicts belief in Jesus to be false.

101
00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:13.160
So we want our students to be able to see that truth is so critically important

102
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:19.160
to furthering our discussions on what it means to believe in Christianity.

103
00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:24.160
So students in small group are going to have a really good chance this week

104
00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:31.160
to discuss and explore how truth opens the door to a life of freedom.

105
00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.160
Because really when we boil this down,

106
00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.160
understanding truth is more than just intellectually understanding what truth is.

107
00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:43.160
It's understanding it so that it leads them to freedom

108
00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:48.803
that they can be in Christ and they can live the life that God has purposed for

109
00:06:48.803 --> 00:06:49.160
them.

110
00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.022
So when we're thinking about truth,

111
00:06:51.022 --> 00:06:54.160
there's two kinds of truth that we're really talking about.

112
00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.160
Now I've talked a lot about the idea of objective truth

113
00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.160
but there's also something we call subjective truth.

114
00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.160
So there's objective and subjective.

115
00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.160
Well what's the difference?

116
00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.160
And oftentimes this is where our view of truth gets sort of confused

117
00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.160
because we mix these two up.

118
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.354
So helping to understand these on your end as well as helping your students to

119
00:07:12.354 --> 00:07:13.160
understand this

120
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.160
is going to be one of those things that's going to help take that wall

121
00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.160
that's dividing you and your students down

122
00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.716
to help them see exactly what it is that you're saying when you're talking about

123
00:07:21.716 --> 00:07:22.160
scripture.

124
00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:26.160
So first let's talk about the idea of subjective truth.

125
00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.160
Well what is the idea of subjective truth?

126
00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.160
But if I say something like,

127
00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:35.160
I love mint chocolate chip ice cream.

128
00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:40.160
But you like another flavor, chocolate let's say.

129
00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:48.160
Is it true that I think mint chocolate chip ice cream is the best kind of ice cream?

130
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.160
Well of course it's true because I think it.

131
00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:56.119
And is it true at the same time that if you think chocolate ice cream is the best

132
00:07:56.119 --> 00:07:57.160
kind of ice cream

133
00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.160
that that is in fact a true statement?

134
00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.160
Well of course it's a true statement because you think it.

135
00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.160
See these are subjective truth statements.

136
00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:12.160
They're true because they're based on my experience and my experience only.

137
00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.160
So it doesn't matter.

138
00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:17.160
And two different things can be both equally true at the same time.

139
00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:22.160
Two different flavors of ice cream can be both true at the exact same time

140
00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.160
because it's completely subjective.

141
00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:28.160
And if I'm not here to say it then this truth statement doesn't matter anymore.

142
00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.160
So it's completely subjective.

143
00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:35.160
On the other side is the idea of objective truth.

144
00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.160
Now objective truth has to do with the object.

145
00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.160
So if you think of it this way,

146
00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.160
subject object.

147
00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.600
Truth statement is about the subject here.

148
00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:53.600
Truth statement is about the object here.

149
00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:54.600
Okay?

150
00:08:54.600 --> 00:09:00.600
So if I'm talking about ice cream I'm talking about how I feel about the ice cream.

151
00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:06.260
But here if I'm talking about something like my shirt,

152
00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.260
if I told you that my shirt was blue you tell me I'm wrong.

153
00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:11.260
Well why?

154
00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.260
Because my shirt isn't blue.

155
00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.260
My shirt is green.

156
00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:19.501
If I told my shirt is black or white or anything but the color that my shirt

157
00:09:19.501 --> 00:09:20.260
actually is

158
00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:21.260
that I'm wrong.

159
00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.260
It's completely independent of my opinion.

160
00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:25.260
It's completely independent of my experience.

161
00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:30.260
Even if I never bought the shirt and it's still on the rack at the store

162
00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:34.915
the shirt is still the color that it is until it ceases to be that shirt and that

163
00:09:34.915 --> 00:09:35.260
color.

164
00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.260
So it doesn't matter.

165
00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:41.260
So it's based on the object, my shirt, not my opinion.

166
00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.260
This is based on my opinion.

167
00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.260
I'm the subject.

168
00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.260
So that's kind of the distinguishing feature.

169
00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:53.260
The problem is that what we do is we lump religion over here.

170
00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:58.260
And we lump Jesus on the side of subjective truth.

171
00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.679
And we say that well I can believe in Jesus subjectively because based on my

172
00:10:02.679 --> 00:10:03.260
experience

173
00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:08.260
I think it's true and it doesn't matter what anybody else thinks.

174
00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:11.884
And it doesn't matter if you disagree because ever somebody else can believe in

175
00:10:11.884 --> 00:10:13.260
something completely different

176
00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.260
and it be equally true.

177
00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.260
But now we go back to John 14.

178
00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:23.260
Jesus said something that is independent of me.

179
00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:27.260
He said something that is an objective truth statement whether it's true or not.

180
00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:31.260
So that puts belief in Jesus on the objective side.

181
00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:35.260
So when we're talking about Jesus, we're talking about Christianity,

182
00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:38.584
we're talking about the way in which the world works and God being creator and all

183
00:10:38.584 --> 00:10:41.260
the things that we're going to talk about for the rest of the year

184
00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:44.260
we're talking about objective truth statements.

185
00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:47.260
They're either true or they're not.

186
00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:50.260
And we have to make sure our students understand that they're here.

187
00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:53.260
It's not a matter of opinion or experience.

188
00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:55.260
It's a matter of reality.

189
00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:04.260
So truth is what corresponds with reality which then leads to freedom.

190
00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:09.280
This is what we want our students to see primarily this week is that understanding

191
00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.260
objective truth,

192
00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:13.260
understanding that truth is often objective,

193
00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:16.260
understanding that belief in Jesus is objective.

194
00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.260
It is how it corresponds and lines up with reality.

195
00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:24.260
And understanding those things is what's going to lead your students to the feeling

196
00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:29.260
and the understanding and the experience of genuine freedom in Christ.

